cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  IndentView: spatially resolved analysis of instrumented
  indentation data
message: >-
  If you use this software in published work, please cite it and
  state the version. Results produced before version 2.3.0 are
  not comparable to later results; see CHANGELOG.md.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohammadreza
    family-names: Vatankhah
    email: mohammadrvatankhah@gmail.com
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # add your ORCID
repository-code: 'https://github.com/rezavtn8/indntviw'
url: 'https://github.com/rezavtn8/indntviw'
abstract: >-
  IndentView is an open-source, browser-based platform for
  spatially resolved analysis of instrumented indentation
  (nanoindentation) data. It renders indentation matrices as
  property maps, supports definition of regions of interest
  directly on the map, and performs group comparisons in which
  the unit of analysis is an explicit choice rather than an
  implicit consequence of how the data were tabulated. All
  statistical routines are verified against published reference
  values in continuous integration. The application runs entirely
  client-side; measurement data never leaves the operator's
  machine.
keywords:
  - nanoindentation
  - instrumented indentation
  - materials characterisation
  - soft tissue mechanics
  - property mapping
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - pseudoreplication
  - scientific visualisation
